WEBVTT

00:35:57.288 --> 00:36:03.079
which is that we build this thing and
at some point somewhat suddenly,

00:36:03.371 --> 00:36:07.663
it's much more powerful than we are, we
haven't really done the full merge yet.

00:36:08.163 --> 00:36:10.996
There's an event horizon there and
it's sort of hard to see to

00:36:10.996 --> 00:36:14.538
the other side of it. Again, lots of
reasons to think it will go OK.

00:36:14.538 --> 00:36:17.163
Lots of reasons to think we won't
even get to that scenario.

00:36:17.704 --> 00:36:18.996
But that is something that.

00:36:20.079 --> 00:36:22.579
I don't think people should brush under
the rug as much as they do,

00:36:22.579 --> 00:36:24.454
it's in the possibility space for sure,

00:36:25.038 --> 00:36:28.329
and in the possibility subspace
of that is one where, like,

00:36:28.538 --> 00:36:31.788
we didn't actually do as good of a job
on the alignment work as we thought.